      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Role in enuresis:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " behavioral modification = first-line; a bed-wetting alarm = the most effective long-term strategy w no organic cause; oral desmopressin (or imipramine) can ↓ nighttime wetting, but results aren't sustained in most pts after stopping; DDAVP is preferable to imipramine (rare sudden death w imipramine)."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Boxed warning:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " severe hyponatremia can cause seizures, coma, resp arrest or death."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
